# Need for Speed - Underground 2 (USA)
#
# Widescreen [restart]
#   Need for Speed - Underground 2 (USA), default.xbe
#   Nemesis2000 (https://github.com/JayYardley/Xbox-Magic-Patches-by-Jay)
#   Tested with hakuX-lr 8921d9d4a1 and RetroArch 1.22.2 (x86-64), headless.
#   A race has a wider 16:9 view with the core's Screen Format set to Widescreen. The HUD remains stretched.
#   A 16:9 view of the 3D scene, with the console's video set to widescreen. The HUD and the menus stay stretched.
#
# 60 fps [restart]
#   Need for Speed - Underground 2 (USA), default.xbe
#   hakuX
#   Tested with hakuX-lr 8921d9d4a1 and RetroArch 1.22.2 (x86-64).
#   Races run at 60 fps (30 unpatched); the race clock counted 93.4 s in 93.7 s (93.6 s unpatched). Checked in one circuit race, headless; not play-tested by hand.
#   Driving at 60 frames a second instead of 30, like the menus, at the game's normal speed. A frame the device doesn't finish in time shows a vblank late.
#
# 128 MB memory [restart]
#   Need for Speed - Underground 2 (USA), default.xbe
#   hakuX-lr
#   Tested with hakuX-lr dbc8b16778 and RetroArch 1.22.2 (x86-64), headless.
#   Raises the game's memory pool from 55 MB to 79 MB, which 720p needs.
#   Set Console RAM to 128 MB and enable the RAM limit patch.
#
# 720p (1280x720) [restart]
#   Need for Speed - Underground 2 (USA), default.xbe
#   hakuX-lr, with the wider view of Nemesis2000's Widescreen patch
#   Tested with hakuX-lr dbc8b16778 and RetroArch 1.22.2 (x86-64), headless, at 1x and 2x render scales.
#   Widescreen 720p with the wider 16:9 view; menus, HUD and movies laid out as in the game's widescreen mode.
#   Enable the 128 MB memory entry above and the core's 720p option; without that option the game returns to the dashboard.

